    "confidence": "low",
    "plain": "The policy presents the \u00a336 billion as savings from cancelling HS2 Phase 2, making it a capital reallocation rather than new net borrowing \u2014 so the direct hit to the debt path is limited. However, questions about whether the 'savings' are fully genuine, and risks of cost overruns from policy instability, create real but unquantifiable fiscal uncertainty.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether the \u00a336 billion genuinely represents freed-up capital or partly repackages already-committed or existing spending \u2014 if the latter, net new borrowing could be higher than stated.",
